{"name":"Purebred","hex":"#67707d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purebred","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having genuine parents of the same breed, usually of an animal."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An animal which has genuine parents of the same breed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purebred"}],"entries":[{"title":"Purebred","blocks":[{"text":"Purebreds are cultivars of an animal species achieved through the process of selective breeding. When the lineage of a purebred animal is recorded, that animal is said to be pedigreed. Purebreds breed true-to-type, which means the progeny of like-to-like purebred parents will carry the same phenotype, or observable characteristics of the parents. A group of like purebreds is called a pure-breeding line or strain."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purebred"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/LaMirage_body07.jpg/500px-LaMirage_body07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/LaMirage_body07.jpg/500px-LaMirage_body07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A purebred Arabian horse.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALaMirage_body07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG/500px-Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG/1280px-Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG/500px-Bram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pure-breed Zwergschnauzer","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABram_Zwergschnauzer.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Chocolate_Persian.jpg/500px-Chocolate_Persian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Chocolate_Persian.jpg/1280px-Chocolate_Persian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Chocolate_Persian.jpg/500px-Chocolate_Persian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Purebred chocolate Persian show cat with \"Grand Champion\" title.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_Persian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Friesian_Stallion.jpg/500px-Friesian_Stallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Friesian_Stallion.jpg/500px-Friesian_Stallion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A Frisian horse (stallion), a breed which earliest known reference is from AD 50 (reign of Roman Emperor Nero) and is pedigree registered since 1879[23]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFriesian_Stallion.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}